# Caching Strategies

## Overview
When and how to use caching (Redis, in-memory) for performance optimization.

## When to Cache

- Read-heavy operations
- Expensive computations
- External API responses
- Database query results

## Redis Caching

**✅ CORRECT:**
```typescript
async getUser(userId: string) {
  const cacheKey = `user:${userId}`;
  const cached = await this.redis.get(cacheKey);
  if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached);
  
  const user = await this.repository.findById(userId);
  await this.redis.setex(cacheKey, 3600, JSON.stringify(user));
  return user;
}
```

## Cache Invalidation

**✅ CORRECT - Invalidate on updates:**
```typescript
async updateUser(userId: string, data: UpdateUserDto) {
  const user = await this.repository.update(userId, data);
  await this.redis.del(`user:${userId}`);
  return user;
}
```

## TTL Strategies

- Short TTL (5-15 min): Frequently changing data
- Medium TTL (1 hour): Moderately changing data
- Long TTL (24 hours): Rarely changing data

